%U A395816 971688764763227907612407,1057198980466907795111869,1574659518193293073896953,1651613100316182634822211,2579882148294177281806591,2681186855821233923845067,3045998278981289844695333
%N A395816 Brier numbers that have at least two minimal distinct covering sets.
%C A395816 From _James Shakarji_, Sep 22 2026: (Start)
%C A395816 The terms a(1)..a(3000) all arise from covering systems of period 720. In each, one side is covered by 3 together with a six-prime subset of {5, 13, 17, 97, 241, 257, 673} with period 48, and the other by 3 together with primes from {7, 11, 13, 19, 31, 37, 41, 61, 73, 109, 151, 331} with period 720. The second minimal covering set arises when a prime not needed by the certificate happens to divide the right terms: e.g., 13 (which has order 12 = 13-1 in the multiplicative group mod 2) is active for every k prime to 13, so it can replace 41, 73, 109 or 151 in a covering set whenever their residue classes coincide.
%C A395816 a(821) = 300803383615580263898123513, a(1446), a(1799), a(2350), a(2442) and a(2463) have four minimal covering sets each and are therefore also in A397300; all other terms up to a(3000) have exactly two. (End)
%H A395816 James Shakarji, <a href="/A395816/b395816.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3000</a> (terms 1..29 from Emilia Gurisatti, with missing terms a(4) and a(17) from James Shakarji).
%H A395816 Emilia Gurisatti, <a href="https://github.com/emiguri/brierdouble/blob/main/brierdouble.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..29 with its covering sets</a>
%H A395816 Wilfrid Keller, <a href="http://www.prothsearch.com/briernums.html">A Collection of Brier Numbers</a>
%H A395816 Carlos Rivera, <a href="https://www.primepuzzles.net/problems/prob_092.htm">Problem 92. Multiple covering sets for Sierpinski and for Riesel integers</a>, The Prime Puzzles & Problems Connection.
%H A395816 James Shakarji, <a href="/A395816/a395816.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3000 with its covering sets</a>
%H A395816 James Shakarji, <a href="/A395816/a395816.py.txt">Sierpinski/Riesel-residue propagation with minimum-weight covers and CRT descent for the generation of Brier numbers with at least two covering sets</a>
%e A395816 For every k >= 1, 216644304573327922644547*2^k + 1 has a divisor in the set {3, 5, 7, 11, 17, 19, 31, 37, 41, 61, 73, 97, 109, 151, 241, 257, 331, 673} and also in the set {3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 31, 37, 61, 73, 97, 109, 151, 241, 257, 331, 673}.
%e A395816 For every k >= 1, 216644304573327922644547*2^k - 1 has a divisor in the set {3, 5, 7, 11, 17, 19, 31, 37, 41, 61, 73, 97, 109, 151, 241, 257, 331, 673} and also in the set {3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 31, 37, 61, 73, 97, 109, 151, 241, 257, 331, 673}. 216644304573327922644547 is therefore in the sequence.
%Y A395816 Cf. A076335, A076336, A076337, A263391, A263392, A397300.
